  "why": "B22, Java. Instantiation is `CALLS` to the created Type (corpus/README.md). Every shape that runs a constructor of an in-repo type is an edge: plain, with arguments, fully qualified, a nested type, an explicit generic, a diamond, an anonymous class of an interface and of an abstract class (the edge goes to the type instantiated), and a returned creation. The refusals are the shapes that look like one and are not: an array creation, a constructor reference, an external generic whose type argument is in-repo, a creation inside a local class's method, constructor chaining, and a same-named type shadowed by an explicit external import.",
